title: pylint E0601 used-before-assignment
authors: pylint-dev
year: 2024
venue: pylint readthedocs
quality: DOCS
url: https://pylint.readthedocs.io/en/latest/user_guide/messages/error/used-before-assignment.html
keywords: used-before-assignment, unbound, local variable, CFG, pylint E0601
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  RULE ID: E0601
  WHAT IT FLAGS: A local variable is used (read) before it is assigned. Includes
    use of += on an uninitialized local variable. Checked by the variables checker.
  FLOW PROPERTY: Intra-procedural control flow analysis. Pylint builds a CFG and
    checks that every use of a local variable has a reaching definition on all paths
    from function entry to the use site. More complete than pyflakes' linear scan.
  KNOWN FALSE POSITIVES:
    - Variables defined in both branches of TYPE_CHECKING conditionals (issue #7368)
    - Assignment expressions (walrus :=) used within the same tuple (issue #3275)
    - Nested try blocks that exhaustively define/raise/return (issue #7350)
    - Type annotations that take assignment via nonlocal (issue #5394)
    - Type hints (issue #8110)
  KNOWN FALSE NEGATIVES:
    - Variable only defined in except clause, read after try/except — false negative
      reported (issue #4761)
  DIFFERS FROM PYFLAKES: Pylint's analysis is more CFG-aware and handles complex
    branching scenarios better than pyflakes' simpler scope-based check.
  CLASSIFICATION: FLOW-NATIVE (CFG + reaching definitions)
  TOOLS: pylint (E0601)
<<<END>>>

