id: 7
ts: 2026-05-29T10:06:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: CodeQL py/unreachable-statement
authors: GitHub Security Lab
year: 2024
venue: CodeQL query help (codeql.github.com)
quality: DOCS
url: https://codeql.github.com/codeql-query-help/python/py-unreachable-statement/
keywords: unreachable code, dead code, CodeQL, CFG, CWE-561
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  QUERY ID: py/unreachable-statement
  SEVERITY: Warning
  PRECISION: Very-high
  TAGS: quality, maintainability, useless-code, CWE-561
  WHAT IT FLAGS: Code statements that cannot be executed during program flow, typically
    appearing after control flow statements like return, break, or continue.
  FLOW PROPERTY: CodeQL builds a full Python CFG where each AstNode maps to zero, one,
    or many ControlFlowNodes. An AstNode with ZERO ControlFlowNodes is unreachable.
    "Any AstNode that is unreachable has no paths flowing through it. Therefore, any
    AstNode without a corresponding ControlFlowNode is unreachable." The query targets
    statement nodes specifically (not all AstNodes) to avoid false positives from
    modules with no source code representation.
  EXAMPLE:
    def my_div(x, y):
        return math.floor(x / y)
        remainder = x - math.floor(x / y) * y  # unreachable — flagged
  DOCUMENTATION NOTE: "This may indicate dead code, or some other error."
  CFG IMPLEMENTATION: ControlFlowNode/AstNode mapping in CodeQL Python library.
    BasicBlock analysis available for aggregated reachability queries.
    strictlyReaches() predicate for inter-block reachability.
  CLASSIFICATION: FLOW-NATIVE (full CFG reachability)
  TOOLS: CodeQL (py/unreachable-statement); pylint (W0101, partial); vulture (partial)
<<<END>>>

