id: 12
ts: 2026-05-29T10:11:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: pyflakes/ruff F401 / pylint W0611 Unused Import
authors: PyCQA, astral-sh, pylint-dev
year: 2024
venue: multiple
quality: DOCS
url: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/unused-import/
keywords: unused import, F401, W0611, dead import, import analysis
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  RULE IDs: F401 (pyflakes/ruff), W0611 (pylint unused-import)
  WHAT THEY FLAG: Import statements where the imported name/module is never referenced
    in the module body. Unused imports create runtime overhead, risk of import cycles,
    and cognitive load.
  FLOW PROPERTY: Scope-level name use tracking. After collecting all imports as
    Importation bindings in the module scope, walk all USE sites. An import with no
    corresponding use is flagged. No CFG required — this is a module-scope name
    presence check. However, ruff needs to handle: re-exports (from x import y as y
    is treated as used), __all__ exports (names in __all__ are treated as used),
    TYPE_CHECKING blocks.
  RUFF F401 OPTIONS:
    - lint.ignore-init-module-imports
    - lint.pyflakes.allowed-unused-imports
    - In __init__.py: suggests exporting via alias or __all__; unsafe fix removes
      third-party/stdlib imports
  PYLINT W0611 SPECIFICS: "Used when an imported module or variable is not used.
    By default, this check is skipped for __init__.py files." Created by variables checker.
  FALSE POSITIVES: Re-exports, side-effect imports (imported for registration/plugin
    effect), TYPE_CHECKING-guarded imports, overload decorators.
  CLASSIFICATION: AST-LINT (scope-level name tracking, no CFG needed)
  TOOLS: ruff (F401), pyflakes (F841), pylint (W0611), CodeQL (py/unused-import)
<<<END>>>

