id: 16
ts: 2026-05-29T10:15:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: pyright reportOptional* — None Dereference / Optional Misuse
authors: Microsoft
year: 2024
venue: pyright configuration docs
quality: DOCS
url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/microsoft/pyright/main/docs/configuration.md
keywords: None dereference, Optional, reportOptionalMemberAccess, reportOptionalSubscript, pyright
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  RULE IDs:
    reportOptionalSubscript — "Attempt to index variables with Optional types."
    reportOptionalMemberAccess — "Attempt to access members of Optional-typed variables."
    reportOptionalCall — "Attempt to call Optional-typed variables."
    reportOptionalIterable — "Optional types used as iterables in for statements."
    reportOptionalContextManager — "Optional types used with with statements."
    reportOptionalOperand — "Optional types as operands to unary or binary operators."
  WHAT THEY FLAG: Any operation on a variable of type T | None (Optional[T]) that
    would raise AttributeError/TypeError at runtime if the value is None. These rules
    collectively implement Python's "strict optional" checking.
  FLOW PROPERTY: TYPE-NARROWING + DATAFLOW. Pyright tracks the type of each variable
    at each program point. After `if x is not None:`, the type of x inside the branch
    is narrowed to T (not None). The reportOptional* rules only fire if the type at the
    use site still includes None (i.e., the None case has NOT been narrowed away by a
    preceding guard check). This requires: (1) type inference to determine that a
    variable has Optional type, (2) type narrowing through conditional branches,
    (3) CFG-aware propagation of narrowed types to use sites.
  DEFAULTS: All reportOptional* rules default to "error" in Basic mode and above.
  RELATION TO MYPY: mypy implements equivalent checking via strict-optional mode
    (--strict-optional, default on since mypy 0.600). mypy's error codes: [index],
    [attr-defined], [operator], [assignment] on Optional values.
  CLASSIFICATION: FLOW-NATIVE (type narrowing requires CFG-based type-state propagation)
  TOOLS: pyright (reportOptional*), mypy (strict-optional), pylint (limited via
    inferred types)
<<<END>>>

