id: 17
ts: 2026-05-29T10:16:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: mypy error codes — possibly-undefined, unreachable, redundant-expr
authors: python/mypy
year: 2024
venue: mypy readthedocs
quality: DOCS
url: https://mypy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/error_code_list2.html
keywords: possibly-undefined, unreachable, redundant-expr, mypy, control flow, optional check
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  ERROR CODES (optional, enabled via --enable-error-code):
    possibly-undefined: "Mypy generates an error if it cannot verify that a variable
      will be defined in all execution paths. Includes situations when a variable
      definition appears in a loop, in a conditional branch, in an except handler, etc."
      Status: disabled by default, must opt in. Known false positive: match statement
      with exhaustive coverage (issue #16992). False negative: potentially unbound
      instance attribute (issue #17837).
    unreachable: (--warn-unreachable) "Generates an error if a statement or expression
      will never be executed. In most cases this is due to incorrect control flow or
      conditional checks that are accidentally always true or false."
    redundant-expr: "Generates an error if an expression is redundant." Catches
      always-true/always-false conditions based on type narrowing — e.g.,
      `if isinstance(x, int) and isinstance(x, str):` is always False.
    truthy-bool: "Warn when the type of an expression in a boolean context does not
      implement __bool__ or __len__."
  ERROR CODES (default):
    return: "If a function has a non-None return type, mypy expects the function always
      explicitly returns a value (or raises an exception)." Control flow analysis to
      ensure all paths return.
    return-value: "Mypy checks that the returned value is compatible with the type
      signature of the function."
  FLOW PROPERTIES:
    possibly-undefined: requires CFG join-point analysis (same as pyright reportPossiblyUnbound)
    unreachable: requires type-state propagation — code is unreachable when type analysis
      determines it cannot be reached (e.g., after isinstance narrowing that covers all cases)
    redundant-expr: requires type narrowing + constant condition detection
    return: requires CFG terminal analysis (all exits must be covered)
  CLASSIFICATION: ALL are FLOW-NATIVE
  TOOLS: mypy (all above codes)
<<<END>>>

