id: 20
ts: 2026-05-29T10:19:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: CodeQL py/unused-local-variable
authors: GitHub Security Lab
year: 2024
venue: CodeQL query help
quality: DOCS
url: https://codeql.github.com/codeql-query-help/python/py-unused-local-variable/
keywords: unused local variable, dead assignment, CodeQL, CWE-563
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  QUERY ID: py/unused-local-variable
  SEVERITY: Recommendation
  PRECISION: Very-high
  CWE: CWE-563
  WHAT IT FLAGS: Local variables assigned but never subsequently read.
  NAMING EXCLUSIONS (not flagged as unused):
    - Names consisting entirely of underscores
    - Names containing "unused"
    - Variables named "dummy" or "empty"
    - Special names __xxx__
  FLOW PROPERTY: Def-use chain analysis. After all assignments to a local name, check
    that at least one USE is reachable from the assignment. For grouped assignments
    (x, y = func()), if ALL variables are unused they are reported together; if any
    is used, all are treated as used (conservative).
  EXAMPLE:
    random_no = write_random_to_file()  # assigned but never read — flagged
    print("A random number was written")
  FALSE POSITIVE HANDLING: Grouped assignments handled specially. Naming conventions
    respected. Very-high precision means minimal false positives.
  CLASSIFICATION: FLOW-NATIVE (requires def-use chain analysis to detect fully
    unreferenced definitions, though simple scope tracking is sufficient for "never
    referenced at all" case)
  TOOLS: CodeQL (py/unused-local-variable), pyflakes (F841), pylint (W0612)
<<<END>>>

