cites:
cited_by:
content:
  RULE ID: W0621 (redefined-outer-name)
  WHAT IT FLAGS: A variable's name hides a name defined in an outer scope or except handler.
    Triggers when function-local variable has same name as module-level variable, or
    function parameter shadows enclosing scope name.
  EXAMPLES: Function parameter `filename` shadowing global `filename`; `app` parameter
    shadowing global `app`.
  KNOWN GAP: W0621 correctly fires for module-level shadowing but DOES NOT report when
    a function-local variable hides one from an enclosing function scope (nonlocal
    variable without nonlocal declaration). Issue #442 tracks this.
  FLOW PROPERTY: Scope-chain analysis. Requires walking the scope stack and comparing
    names at each level. No CFG needed — purely lexical scope analysis.
  CLASSIFICATION: AST-LINT (lexical scope analysis)
  TOOLS: pylint (W0621); ruff (A001 variable-shadows-builtin, A002 argument-shadows-builtin)
<<<END>>>

