id: 25
ts: 2026-05-29T10:24:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: Meta Pysa (Pyre) — Interprocedural Taint Analysis
authors: Meta Engineering
year: 2020
venue: engineering.fb.com / pyre-check.org
quality: INDUSTRY
url: https://pyre-check.org/docs/pysa-basics/
keywords: Pysa, Pyre, taint analysis, interprocedural, dataflow, sources, sinks, sanitizers
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  TOOL: Pysa (integrated into Pyre, Meta's Python type checker)
  APPROACH: Interprocedural taint analysis. Tracks flows from SOURCES (origins of
    untrusted data, e.g. HTTP request parameters) to SINKS (dangerous operations,
    e.g. eval(), SQL exec).
  SOURCES/SINKS/SANITIZERS: Declared in taint.config JSON and .pysa model files using
    annotations: TaintSource[Name], TaintSink[Name], @Sanitize, TaintInTaintOut.
  RULES: Connect specific source kinds to sink kinds. A rule for SQL injection flags
    user-controlled data flowing into SQL queries.
  INTERPROCEDURAL: Propagates taint across function calls. If tainted data flows
    into a function, return value inherits taint (conservative when source unavailable).
  FLOW PROPERTY: Full interprocedural dataflow (taint propagation). Models forward
    data flow: taint propagates through assignments, arithmetic, string formatting,
    indexing. Taint is tracked via reaching-definitions extended with taint labels.
  AT-EXIT SINKS (Semgrep Pro equivalent): Pysa can flag resource leaks framed as
    "taint reaching function exit without being released" — though this is primarily
    used for security (secret reaching log) not resource management.
  FALSE POSITIVES: When taint flows into functions without source code, conservatively
    assumes return value inherits taint — can generate false positives.
  STATUS: Open source on GitHub (facebook/Pyre-check). Actively maintained as of 2024.
    Used internally at Meta to find vulnerabilities in large-scale Python codebase.
  DIFFERS FROM PYRIGHT/MYPY: Pysa focuses on security data flows, not type correctness.
  CLASSIFICATION: FLOW-NATIVE (full interprocedural taint dataflow)
  TOOLS: Pysa (Meta/pyre-check)
<<<END>>>

