id: 29
ts: 2026-05-29T10:32:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: bandit B110 try_except_pass and B112 try_except_continue (Exception Swallowing)
authors: PyCQA
year: 2024
venue: bandit readthedocs
quality: DOCS
url: https://bandit.readthedocs.io/en/latest/plugins/b110_try_except_pass.html
keywords: exception swallowing, try-except-pass, bandit, B110, B112, CWE-703
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  RULE IDs: B110 (try_except_pass), B112 (try_except_continue)
  B110 DESCRIPTION: "It is possible to catch an exception and silently ignore it. This
    pattern is considered bad practice in general, but also represents a potential
    security issue. A larger than normal volume of errors from a service can indicate an
    attempt is being made to disrupt or interfere with it. Thus errors should, at the
    very least, be logged."
  B112 DESCRIPTION: Same as B110 but for `except: continue` pattern — exception caught
    and execution continues in the loop.
  CONFIGURATION:
    check_typed_exception (bool, default True): When False, ignores typed exceptions
    (except ZeroDivisionError: pass), only flagging untyped or broad catches.
  SEVERITY: Low
  CONFIDENCE: High
  CWE: CWE-703 (Improper Check or Handling of Exceptional Conditions)
  WHAT IT DETECTS: AST pattern: try block with except clause whose body contains only
    `pass` (B110) or only `continue` (B112). Does NOT check whether exception is
    re-raised on any path — purely syntactic.
  FLOW PROPERTY NEEDED FOR FULL DETECTION: Detecting "exception swallowed and not
    re-raised on any path" requires flow analysis of except body — checking that
    no path through the except handler executes a bare `raise`. This is FLOW-NATIVE.
    Bandit's version is AST-LINT (just `pass` literal in handler).
  PYLINT W0706 (try-except-raise): Detects the OPPOSITE anti-pattern — raise as
    FIRST statement in except block (useless, immediately re-raises same exception).
  FALSE POSITIVES: Legitimate uses of silent exception suppression (e.g., optional
    feature availability checks: try: import rapidjson as json; except ImportError: pass).
  CLASSIFICATION: AST-LINT (syntactic pass/continue in handler)
  TOOLS: bandit (B110, B112), pylint (W0702 bare-except, W0703 broad-except),
    ruff (E722, BLE001), CodeQL (py/empty-except)
<<<END>>>

