id: 30
ts: 2026-05-29T10:33:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: CodeQL py/exit-from-finally (break/return in finally suppresses exceptions)
authors: GitHub Security Lab
year: 2024
venue: CodeQL query help
quality: DOCS
url: https://codeql.github.com/codeql-query-help/python/py-exit-from-finally/
keywords: finally block, return in finally, break in finally, exception suppression, CWE-584
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  QUERY ID: py/exit-from-finally
  SEVERITY: Warning
  PRECISION: Medium
  CWE: CWE-584
  TAGS: quality, reliability, correctness
  WHAT IT FLAGS: break or return statements inside finally blocks. "Causes the try-finally
    block to exit immediately discarding the exception."
  TECHNICAL BEHAVIOR: When a finally block contains return or break, Python exits the
    finally block via that statement. Any in-flight exception (from try or except block)
    is silently discarded. This is a CONTROL FLOW escape that suppresses exceptions.
  FLOW PROPERTY: Syntactic — detecting presence of return/break in finally body. The
    EFFECT is a flow property (exception suppression via control-flow escape), but the
    detection itself is structural: is there a return/break inside a finally clause?
  RELATED RULE: flake8-bugbear B012 (same pattern); ruff B012 (jump-statement-in-finally)
  FALSE POSITIVE NOTES: B012 has known false positives when break is in a loop INSIDE
    the finally block (issue #106 in flake8-bugbear) — the break exits the inner loop,
    not the finally block.
  PEP 601: PEP 601 proposed to FORBID return/break/continue breaking out of finally,
    indicating this is a recognized anti-pattern.
  CLASSIFICATION: AST-LINT for detection (structural), FLOW-NATIVE for understanding
    the semantic effect (exception path suppression).
  TOOLS: CodeQL (py/exit-from-finally), flake8-bugbear (B012), ruff (B012),
    pylint (W0150 break-in-finally, W0641 consider-using-with)
<<<END>>>

