id: 31
ts: 2026-05-29T10:34:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: CodeQL py/unreachable-except (Unreachable Except Block due to Exception Order)
authors: GitHub Security Lab
year: 2024
venue: CodeQL query help
quality: DOCS
url: https://codeql.github.com/codeql-query-help/python/py-unreachable-except/
keywords: unreachable except, exception ordering, superclass, except order, CodeQL
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  QUERY ID: py/unreachable-except
  SEVERITY: Error
  PRECISION: (high implied by error severity)
  WHAT IT FLAGS: Exception handlers that can never execute because a preceding,
    more general except block will always catch the exception first.
    "Python searches the except blocks in source code order until it finds a matching
    except block for the exception." When a superclass exception handler appears before
    a subclass handler, the subclass handler becomes unreachable.
  EXAMPLE:
    def incorrect_except_order(val):
        try: val.attr
        except Exception: print("Exception")
        except AttributeError: print("AttributeError")  # Never executes — unreachable!
  FLOW PROPERTY: Exception type hierarchy analysis + exception handler ordering.
    Requires knowing that Exception is a superclass of AttributeError (MRO lookup)
    and that Python matches from top to bottom. The "unreachable" property is a CFG
    property: the except AttributeError node has no incoming exception-flow edges that
    are not already caught by except Exception.
  CLASSIFICATION: FLOW-NATIVE (exception type hierarchy + exception propagation flow)
  FIX: Reorder except blocks from most specific to most general.
  TOOLS: CodeQL (py/unreachable-except); pylint has some coverage
    via exception-checker; pyflakes does not detect this.
<<<END>>>

