title: pylint W0631 loop-variable + B023 closure-variable-capture — Detector Classification Summary
authors: pylint-dev, PyCQA
year: 2024
venue: composite
quality: DOCS
url: https://pylint.readthedocs.io/en/stable/user_guide/messages/warning/undefined-loop-variable.html
keywords: loop variable, undefined-loop-variable, closure capture, late binding, B023, W0631
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  NOTE: This record consolidates related loop-variable detectors for comparison.
  W0631 (pylint undefined-loop-variable):
    SCOPE: Flags use of for-loop variable AFTER loop exits, when loop might not execute
    FLOW PROPERTY: Requires knowing variable is loop-only + possibly empty iterable
  B007 (bugbear / ruff):
    "Loop control variable not used within the loop body" — should start with _
    SCOPE: Flags unused loop variable (wasteful iteration variable name)
    CLASSIFICATION: AST-LINT
  B023 (bugbear / ruff):
    "Functions defined inside a loop must not use variables redefined in the loop"
    SCOPE: Closure captures loop variable (late-binding gotcha)
    CLASSIFICATION: AST-LINT (syntactic scope capture detection)
  py/loop-variable-capture (CodeQL):
    SCOPE: Same as B023 but also verifies closure is CALLED after loop
    CLASSIFICATION: FLOW-NATIVE (call-site + scope analysis)
  py/unused-loop-variable (CodeQL):
    SCOPE: for-loop iteration variable never used in loop body
    SEVERITY: Error / High precision
    CLASSIFICATION: AST-LINT (similar to B007 but labeled Error, not Warning)
  SUMMARY TABLE:
    W0631    post-loop use of possibly-unbound variable      FLOW-NATIVE
    B007     loop var not used in body (wasteful)            AST-LINT
    B023     closure captures loop var (late binding)        AST-LINT (partial)
    py/loop-variable-capture   closure captures + called after loop   FLOW-NATIVE
    py/unused-loop-variable    loop var unused in body       AST-LINT (Error severity)
  TOOLS: pylint (W0631), bugbear/ruff (B007, B023), CodeQL (py/loop-variable-capture,
    py/unused-loop-variable)
<<<END>>>

