id: 35
ts: 2026-05-29T10:38:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: mypy return / return-value error codes (Missing / Inconsistent Return)
authors: python/mypy
year: 2024
venue: mypy readthedocs
quality: DOCS
url: https://mypy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/error_code_list.html
keywords: return, return-value, missing return, inconsistent return, mypy, CFG
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  ERROR CODES:
    return: "If a function has a non-None return type, mypy expects that the function
      always explicitly returns a value (or raises an exception)." Requires control flow
      analysis to ensure all code paths return.
      NOTE: This is the mypy equivalent of pylint R1710 inconsistent-return-statements.
    return-value: "Mypy checks that the returned value is compatible with the type
      signature of the function." Type-level check, not primarily flow-based.
    empty-body: "Checks functions and methods with empty bodies that have non-trivial
      return types, requiring path analysis to detect missing implementations."
  FLOW PROPERTY: `return` code requires: build function CFG; find all terminal nodes
    (CFG exits); check each is either explicit return-with-value or raise/NoReturn call.
    Equivalent to R1710 in terms of CFG requirements.
  ISSUE #13203: Optional return type requires explicit return statement for non-empty
    function — mypy incorrectly requires explicit return for Optional[T] return type
    with bare `return` (known bug).
  ISSUE #11656: Optional return type not correctly handled when function returns without
    None value — returns without value in Optional[T] context.
  STRICT OPTIONAL:
    mypy's `--strict-optional` (default since 0.600) enables None-safety. Equivalent
    to pyright's reportOptional* family of checks. Any Optional[T] variable used without
    None check triggers type errors.
  CLASSIFICATION: FLOW-NATIVE (return code requires CFG terminal analysis)
  TOOLS: mypy (return, return-value), pyright (reportReturnType), pylint (R1710)
<<<END>>>

