id: 39
ts: 2026-05-29T10:50:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: pylint W0150 lost-exception (return/break in finally silences exception)
authors: pylint-dev
year: 2024
venue: pylint readthedocs
quality: DOCS
url: https://pylint.readthedocs.io/en/latest/user_guide/messages/warning/lost-exception.html
keywords: lost-exception, finally, return, break, exception silenced, W0150
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  RULE ID: W0150 (lost-exception)
  WHAT IT FLAGS: "break or return statement found inside the finally clause of a
    try...finally block: the exceptions raised in the try clause will be silently
    swallowed instead of being re-raised."
  EXAMPLE:
    def calculate_speed(distance, time):
        try:
            return distance / time
        except ZeroDivisionError as e:
            raise FasterThanLightError() from e
        finally:
            return 299792458  # W0150: FasterThanLightError is lost!
  FLOW PROPERTY: Control flow analysis of finally blocks. Detects whether the finally
    block contains a return or break that would cause exception to be swallowed.
    Specifically: "if any path through the finally block exits via return/break, the
    exception in flight is discarded." This is a SHALLOW CFG property: is there a
    return/break in the finally clause body?
  EQUIVALENT RULES: CodeQL py/exit-from-finally (same pattern), ruff B012 (same pattern)
  CLASSIFICATION: AST-LINT (syntactic: return/break present in finally). The semantic
    consequence is a flow property (exception suppression).
  TOOLS: pylint (W0150), CodeQL (py/exit-from-finally), ruff/bugbear (B012)
<<<END>>>

