id: 43
ts: 2026-05-29T10:54:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: ruff ARG001/ARG002 and pylint W0613 — Unused Function/Method Arguments
authors: astral-sh, pylint-dev
year: 2024
venue: ruff docs, pylint docs
quality: DOCS
url: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/unused-function-argument/
keywords: unused argument, ARG001, ARG002, W0613, function parameter
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  RULE IDs: ARG001 (ruff unused-function-argument), ARG002 (unused-method-argument),
    W0613 (pylint unused-argument)
  WHAT THEY FLAG: Function or method parameters that are defined but never referenced
    in the function body.
  FLOW PROPERTY: Scope-level name use tracking. After collecting all parameters as
    name bindings, check whether each is referenced in the function body. No CFG needed
    — purely scope-level analysis.
  FALSE POSITIVES (EXTENSIVE):
    - pytest fixtures: fixture name in test signature but not used directly (issue #4673)
    - Liskov substitution: argument kept for interface compatibility (issue #15952)
    - @singledispatch: base function args often unused (issue #18654)
    - Stub functions that only raise NotImplementedError
    - *args, **kwargs pattern where args is ignored
    - @typing.override decorated methods (ruff ARG002 exempts these)
  FIX: Prefix argument name with _ to indicate intentional non-use.
  CLASSIFICATION: AST-LINT (scope-level: is name in function params but not referenced?)
  TOOLS: ruff (ARG001, ARG002), pylint (W0613)
<<<END>>>

