id: 44
ts: 2026-05-29T10:55:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: ruff RUF059 unused-unpacked-variable / F841 unused-variable
authors: astral-sh
year: 2024
venue: ruff docs
quality: DOCS
url: https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/unused-unpacked-variable/
keywords: unused-unpacked-variable, RUF059, F841, unpacking, dead assignment
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  RULE ID: RUF059 (unused-unpacked-variable); related: F841 (unused-variable)
  WHAT IT FLAGS (RUF059): Variables in unpacked assignments that are never referenced.
    Example: `x, y = get_pair(); return x` — y is never used. Flag y.
    "A variable that is defined but never used can confuse readers."
  DIFFERENCE FROM F841: F841 handles regular assignments (x = 1 and x is never used).
    RUF059 handles tuple/list unpacking specifically. They were split because detection
    and fix patterns differ.
  EXAMPLE:
    Problem: x, y = get_pair(); return x  # y unused
    Fix:     x, _ = get_pair(); return x  # or simply x, _ = ...
  RESPECTS: lint.dummy-variable-rgx — variables matching pattern (e.g., _ or _unused)
    are excluded from flagging.
  ADDED: ruff v0.13.0
  SCOPE: Only within function scopes.
  CLASSIFICATION: AST-LINT (scope-level: is unpacked name referenced in scope?)
    Not full liveness — only checks "ever referenced at all" not "last write unreached."
  TOOLS: ruff (RUF059, F841), pylint (W0612)
<<<END>>>

