id: 45
ts: 2026-05-29T10:56:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: pylint W0707 raise-missing-from (Exception Chaining / Missing from Clause)
authors: pylint-dev
year: 2024
venue: pylint readthedocs
quality: DOCS
url: https://pylint.readthedocs.io/en/stable/user_guide/messages/warning/raise-missing-from.html
keywords: raise-missing-from, exception chaining, W0707, from clause, exception context
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  RULE ID: W0707 (raise-missing-from)
  WHAT IT FLAGS: A `raise` statement inside an `except` block that doesn't use the
    `from` keyword to chain exceptions. When raising a new exception inside an except
    block, using `raise NewError() from original_error` (or `from None` to suppress)
    preserves the exception chain context. Without `from`, Python automatically adds
    "During handling of the above exception, another exception occurred" context.
  FLOW PROPERTY: Needs to know: (1) raise is inside an except block (scope/AST check),
    (2) the raise doesn't use `from` keyword. This is AST-level checking — no CFG.
  CLASSIFICATION: AST-LINT
  TOOLS: pylint (W0707), ruff (B904 abstract-base-class-without-abstract-method
    equivalent — no exact match; TRY200 is related but removed), flake8-bugbear (B904)
<<<END>>>


SOURCE
id: 46
ts: 2026-05-29T11:00:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: pylint E0601 / E0602 / E0606 — Three-Way Distinction: undefined vs before-assignment vs possibly-before-assignment
authors: pylint-dev
year: 2024
venue: pylint readthedocs
quality: DOCS
url: https://pylint.readthedocs.io/en/latest/user_guide/messages/error/used-before-assignment.html
keywords: E0601, E0602, E0606, undefined variable, used before assignment, possibly used before assignment
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  THREE DISTINCT RULE IDs:
    E0602 (undefined-variable): "Undefined variable %r accessed." Variable has NEVER
      been defined in any accessible scope. Equivalent to pyflakes F821.
    E0601 (used-before-assignment): "Local variable %r referenced before assignment."
      Variable IS assigned somewhere in the function but the assignment hasn't occurred
      yet at the point of USE. DEFINITE use-before-def on all paths.
    E0606 (possibly-used-before-assignment): "Possibly using variable %r before
      assignment." Variable might be used before assignment DEPENDING ON control flow
      — only on some paths does the assignment occur before the use.
  KEY BEHAVIORAL DETAILS (from docs):
    E0601: "Assignments in try blocks are assumed not to have occurred when evaluating
      associated except/finally blocks, and assignments in except blocks are assumed
      not to have occurred when evaluating statements outside the block, except when the
      associated try block contains a return statement."
    NOTE: This means pylint DOES model try/except control flow for E0601.
  E0606 FALSE POSITIVES (known issues):
    - Doesn't understand never-returning functions (NoReturn) — issue #9627
    - Doesn't understand negation of conditionals (issue #9628)
    - E0606 doesn't understand validation done in external function (issue #9715)
    - False positive for pytest.skip and other NoReturn functions (issue #9674)
  FLOW PROPERTY:
    E0602: AST-LINT (scope-level name presence)
    E0601: FLOW-NATIVE (CFG reaching definitions — definite path analysis)
    E0606: FLOW-NATIVE (CFG join-point analysis — may-reach analysis)
  TOOLS: pylint (E0601, E0602, E0606); pyright (reportUnboundVariable for E0602/E0601,
    reportPossiblyUnbound for E0606); mypy (possibly-undefined for E0606);
    pyflakes (F821 for E0602, F823 for E0601)
<<<END>>>

