id: 47
ts: 2026-05-29T11:01:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: ruff CFG Implementation Status — Issue #17065 and PR #17064
authors: astral-sh (dylwil3 et al.)
year: 2025
venue: GitHub astral-sh/ruff
quality: CODE
url: https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/issues/17065
keywords: ruff CFG, control flow graph, unreachable code, ruff liveness, implementation status
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  STATUS: Active development as of March 2025. PR #17064 "Reimplement the control flow
    graph" was being merged incrementally.
  SCOPE: Re-implementation of ruff's CFG for "finer analyses and improve correctness
    of some lint rules."
  IMPLEMENTATION PLAN:
    - CFG struct and builder setup with visualization and snapshot testing
    - Basic jumps (return and raise)
    - Loops (for and while with continue and break)
    - Switch statements (if and match)
  CURRENT STATE: "Implementation currently being a maximal over-approximation where
    no control flow is modeled and all statements are counted as reachable."
    i.e., ruff currently does NOT have a true CFG for most rules — most ruff rules
    are AST-based or scope-based, not flow-graph-based.
  SIGNIFICANCE FOR pflow: This confirms that ruff's existing rules (F841, F401, B-rules)
    are predominantly AST-LINT, not FLOW-NATIVE. True CFG-based detectors in ruff
    are pending the CFG reimplementation.
  TOOLS: ruff (tracking issue for CFG)
<<<END>>>

SOURCE
id: 48
ts: 2026-05-29T11:02:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: pyright Type Narrowing — CFG-Based Type State Propagation
authors: Microsoft (Eric Traut)
year: 2024
venue: pyright/docs/type-concepts-advanced.md
quality: DOCS
url: https://github.com/microsoft/pyright/blob/main/docs/type-concepts-advanced.md
keywords: type narrowing, FlowNode, CFG, isinstance, assignment narrowing, pyright
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  MECHANISM: Pyright uses "type narrowing" to track the type of expressions based on
    code flow. The implementation uses FlowNode analysis — pyright builds a FlowGraph
    (CFG variant) and propagates type state through it.
  NARROWING FORMS:
    - isinstance(val, int): narrows val to int inside if-block, str in else-block
    - `val is None`: narrows to None (if branch) / non-None (else branch)
    - Aliased conditional: `c = a is not None; if c: ...` — c used in conditional
      also narrows the type of a.
    - Assignment narrowing: assigning int to float|str|complex narrows type to int
      at that assignment point.
  JOIN BEHAVIOR: "Once the code flow of a conditional block merges with the main body,
    the narrowed type becomes a union of the possible types from both branches because
    the type checker cannot statically predict whether the conditional block will execute."
  Special handling: Any is NOT narrowed except for isinstance/issubclass/class match.
  UNREACHABLE DETECTION: Code becomes unreachable when narrowed type becomes Never.
    Example: `if isinstance(x, int) and isinstance(x, str):`  — x can't be both int
    and str, so this condition is always False (redundant-expr/mypy or unreachable in pyright).
  IMPLEMENTATION LAYER: Pyright is unique among Python linters in building a full
    CFG (via FlowNode analysis) to drive not just type narrowing but also unbound
    variable detection (reportPossiblyUnbound), unreachable code (reportUnreachable),
    and Optional safety (reportOptional*).
  CLASSIFICATION: FLOW-NATIVE (full CFG with type-state lattice)
  TOOLS: pyright (type narrowing infrastructure powers all diagnostics)
<<<END>>>

