GAPS
- Dead store (last-assignment-never-read) detector: no mainstream Python linter implements full
  liveness-based dead-store detection (pylint issue #5838 is open). Only beniget library
  provides def-use chains needed for this; no standalone checker ships it.
- Pyflakes possibly-unbound for try/finally: pyflakes issue #236 and mypy issue #17387
  both track this gap — the "variable assigned in try-body, read in finally, before assignment"
  case is NOT reliably detected by any mainstream tool.
- Pyflakes does NOT detect the Python 3 "except variable erasure" case (issue #345).
- pylint E0606 does not understand NoReturn functions (#9627, #9628) — false positives.
- Full post-dominance resource-leak detector: no Python linter (other than CodeQL/semgrep Pro)
  implements the full post-dominance property for acquire/release checking. pylint R1732 is
  a shallow heuristic only.
- Full exception-swallowing flow detector (no re-raise on any except-body path): only CodeQL
  implements this; bandit/pylint only check syntactic `pass` or `except:` patterns.
- Ruff does NOT have a true CFG as of early 2025 — most rules are AST-based (confirmed by
  ruff issue #17065 / PR #17064 tracking the reimplementation).
- Scalpel framework (Python CFG builder from arxiv 2202.11840): could not fetch PDF content —
  gap in coverage of this Python CFG library.
- bandit: full rule catalog with precise descriptions not found — only B110, B112 details
  confirmed. B001-B4xx range mentioned but individual rule descriptions not exhaustively fetched.
- Inter-procedural dead-store detection (assignment in caller, never read by caller or callee):
  no Python linter performs interprocedural liveness; only Pysa/CodeQL could approximate.
- True "redundant re-assignment" (x = expr1; ... x = expr2, first assignment never read):
  distinct from "never used at all" — no tool implements this correctly for Python.
